3. Starter Plan
   Starter is the default plan and is provided at no charge for up to two
   clusters, without a fixed expiration date, subject to this License.
   A plan applies to the registered billing organization associated with a
   Platform installation. Its cluster allowance is shared across all projects
   and environments in that installation. Each managed PostgreSQL cluster counts
   once, regardless of its number of nodes or databases. Deleted clusters are
   excluded from the count.
   After a paid subscription expires or is canceled, you may continue under
   Starter only if your cluster count is within the Starter allowance and the
   Autobase Billing service authorizes Starter access. If your cluster count
   exceeds that allowance, you must renew or obtain an appropriate paid
   subscription to continue using the Software. A switch to Starter does not
   waive outstanding charges or override termination for breach of this License.
   Use beyond the Starter cluster allowance requires an active paid subscription
   with a sufficient cluster allowance. Support services are governed by their
   separate terms.

